before** parent effects, so a screen's paint stamp is *always* less than or equal to the watchdog's entry stamp. **The comparison could only ever produce false accusations.**\n\n### Fix — paint is liveness, not freshness\n\nScreens now register when they paint and deregister when they unmount:\n\n```ts\nuseEffect(() => {\n  markScreenPainted('/home');\n  return () => markScreenUnmounted('/home');\n}, []);\n```\n\n```ts\nexport function hasRouteFailedToPaint(route: string): boolean {\n  if (!isRouteInstrumented(route)) return false;\n  return !isRoutePainted(route);   // no timestamps, nothing to race\n}\n```\n\nA mounted screen that rendered content is **never** accused, however long ago it painted. A route that renders nothing holds no record and is still caught — and a blank re-entry is still caught, because the previous visit cleared its record on unmount. The detection I built this for survives; the false positive cannot recur.\n\n## Defect 2 — the recovery button navigated Home onto Home, then went blank for 14 seconds\n\n```ts\nrouter.replace('/(tabs)/home');   // while pathname was ALREADY /home\n```\n\nReplacing the accused route with itself is a no-op that leaves the identical view on screen. Your frames 12-40 measured `rgb(12,8,14)` — `#0A0A0F`, `Colors.background` — an empty container for 14 straight seconds.\n\nIt also did this:\n\n```ts\ndismissedRouteRef.current = pathname;   // pinned forever\n```\n\nOne tap on **Go to Home** made Home permanently unjudgeable for the rest of the process.\n\n### Fix\n\n- Recovery detects it is already on the accused route and bounces through the root so the tab tree genuinely re-resolves and the screen actually remounts.\n- A dismissal now suppresses only the current stay on that route; leaving it re-arms the watchdog.\n\n## Permanent guards — 7 new tests (`Defect 3` block)\n\n- a mounted Home that painted long ago is never flagged, however long ago\n- **the printed contradiction is now unrepresentable**: a route reported as painted can never simultaneously be accused\n- the blank check contains no entry timestamp at all (asserted against the source)\n- both screens deregister their paint on unmount\n- login reports the router pathname `/login`, so its route key actually matches\n- recovery never navigates the accused route onto itself\n- a dismissal is cleared once the user leaves that route\n\nThe v1.10.23 detection tests were kept and rewritten against liveness — a blank Home is still caught even though login already painted.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `runChecks` (TypeScript + lint + structure): **0 errors**\n- Home + routing + crash-shield suites: **40 pass / 0 fail**\n- Full suite: **1186 pass**, 3 pre-existing unrelated failures (unchanged)\n- Gradle: **BUILD SUCCESSFUL**\n\nVerified inside the shipped bundle: stamp `1.10.24 (122)`, `markScreenUnmounted` and `isRoutePainted` present, `(tabs)/(home)` still absent, and every prior layer intact (`Screen failed to load`, `IVX Runtime Error`, `Previous Crash Detected`, `IVX Render Error`, `invalid_credentials`, `rate_limited`, `watchdog-go-home`).\n\nversionName 1.10.24 / versionCode 122\nSHA256: `5512ddcd1462c9d523d848e314f4658eb4ef21992fd7ea121633ac20defa4a79`"
